=== HINT 1: strcpy fix ===
strncpy copies at most n chars but does NOT guarantee null termination.
Always add it manually:
  strncpy(dst, src, sizeof(dst) - 1);
  dst[sizeof(dst) - 1] = '\0';

=== HINT 2: strcat fix ===
strncat appends at most n chars (it DOES null-terminate):
  strncat(dst, src, sizeof(dst) - strlen(dst) - 1);
The -1 leaves room for the null terminator.

=== HINT 3: sprintf fix ===
snprintf writes at most n bytes including the null terminator:
  snprintf(result, sizeof(result), "Value = %d and ...", value);
Excess characters are silently truncated - the buffer stays safe.

=== HINT 4 (SPOILER) ===
// strcpy fix:
strncpy(dst, long_src, BUFSIZE - 1);
dst[BUFSIZE - 1] = '\0';

// strcat fix:
strncat(greeting, ", World! Extra overflow text here.",
        BUFSIZE - strlen(greeting) - 1);

// sprintf fix:
snprintf(result, BUFSIZE, "Value = %d and some extra padding text!!!", value);
